## C. Stored vs Effective State

Stored state is the persisted global configuration: enabled flag, scope, mode, activation time, expiration time, affected assets, metadata, version, and audit relation.

Effective state is computed at runtime:

```text
stored enabled=true
expires_at = T
now > T
→ effective status = expired/inactive
```

Safest architecture remains:

```text
Stored state
    ↓
Central effective-state evaluator
    ↓
Consumers
```

Expiration should not require a physical database update to become effective. Cleanup/reset can be a separate operation. This avoids stale stored rows remaining active merely because no request performed cleanup.

