## E. Versioning / Conflict Strategy

Global control should have a version/revision concept.

It protects against:

```text
Admin A reads version 10
Admin B saves version 11
Admin A submits stale version 10
```

Required strategy: optimistic conflict detection is the safer design for administrative global control. Last-write-wins is dangerous because broad market/trade policies can be accidentally overwritten.

Operations needing version checks:

- Global create/update/disable/restore.
- Emergency state change.
- Scope or expiration change.
- Pair/global conflict-sensitive admin changes if unified later.

Conflict definition:

- Submitted version differs from stored version at write time.
- Stored effective state changed between form load and submit.
- Expiration/activation changed materially.

Outcome for stale writes: reject with refresh requirement, unless product explicitly chooses last-write-wins.

