## Y. Data Integrity Invariants

- Pending trade cannot receive multiple final settlements.
- One settlement cannot create multiple balance credits.
- Successful trade creation requires corresponding balance deduction.
- Failed trade creation must not deduct balance.
- One authoritative effective global policy exists per evaluation.
- Expired state cannot remain effective merely because cleanup did not run.
- Successful mandatory control change cannot be unaudited.
- Frontend state cannot authorize backend action.
- Already-settled trades cannot be modified by later global/pair changes.
- Trade opening and settlement must be server-authoritative.
- Pair controls and trade overrides must not silently change priority.
- Referral commission must not duplicate for one trade.

