## AE. Security / Abuse Boundary

Safety requirements:

- Global control actions require authenticated admin.
- Broad-scope or emergency actions should require explicit confirmation.
- Stale admin writes should be conflict-detected.
- Duplicate admin requests should be idempotent or rejected.
- Invalid/malformed state must be rejected.
- Unauthorized users cannot bypass global restrictions through crafted POSTs.
- Frontend disable/status is informational only.
- All successful global-control changes must be auditable.
- Do not create hidden or covert user-outcome manipulation.
- Global controls must be explicit platform policy with visible admin accountability.
- Product must define whether settlement-affecting global policies are allowed at all.

